  "unit": "u06-bazaar",
  "title": "Haggling",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Bargaining is normal in a bazaar (not in fixed-price shops or supermarkets). Three chunks get you a long way:\n\n- **দাম একটু কম রাখেন।** — 'Lower the price a little, please.' (lit. 'keep the price a little less')\n- **এত দাম কেন?** — 'Why so expensive?'\n- **শেষ দাম কত?** — 'What's your final price?'\n\n**রাখেন** (*rakhen*) is the polite command of 'keep'; with a price it means 'make it…': **দুইশ টাকা রাখেন** 'make it 200 taka'. Standard/Kolkata: **রাখুন**.\n\nTo say no, **লাগবে না** ('I don't need it') is polite and final. To agree: **ঠিক আছে** 'OK'.\n\nNegation of adjectives is easy in speech: just add **না** — **ভালো না** 'not good'.",
